- agent: agent-c
- branch: agent/c/m4-w6-bridge-core
- task: TASK-070
- summary: |
    Implemented HLAFederate.run/step_once/deliver_external in
    pysdk/pyjevsim_bridge/time_advance.py per docs/agent-c-pysdk.md §4.4.

    Design notes:
      - step_once() drains a pending-external queue first; if non-empty,
        it dispatches each (FOM class -> in-port) via external_transition
        and skips the internal cycle (per §4.4 "external arrived
        earlier than ta").
      - Otherwise: read ta, NER for now+ta, drain fed.events() until
        TimeAdvanceGrant. ReceiveInteractions arriving in flight buffer
        into the same queue. Grant arriving with externals in queue
        (or grant.time < t_request) skips the internal phase.
      - Internal cycle: output_handler() -> for each port mapped to a
        FOM class, send_interaction(class_name, parameters={"_payload": p})
        -> internal_transition. Payload pass-through is cut-1; full
        FOM-driven encoding is W7's territory.
      - _now is updated to grant.time at the end of every cycle.
      - run(ticks=N) opens connection (or uses caller-supplied), joins,
        runs N step_once calls, resigns on exit (deterministic via
        try/finally + nested async with).
      - step_once also lazy-initialises the federate so spec tests can
        call it without going through run(). aclose() releases the
        lazy resources; idempotent.
      - deliver_external() is the test/integration seam; production
        traffic from fed.events() converges on the same drain path.

    Auxiliary change to pysdk/tests/spec/m4/_fakes/fake_rti_server.py:
    extended record() to auto-synthesise a TimeAdvanceGrant(time) into
    events_for(federate_handle) on next_message_request — the fake has
    no scheduler. Existing tests remain back-compat (the explicit grant
    push and auto-grant carry the same time; iterators read first event
    only).

